    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of the lineup. With an elite score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an ideal matchup against Matthews, whose 4.32 xERA provides a soft landing, while a favorable platoon advantage and a slow delivery from the mound create a high-probability environment for stolen bases\u2014a critical factor for our 5x5 Roto needs. Alongside him, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Drake Baldwin** (67.38) represent our most efficient leverage plays. **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup against Lowder, while **Drake Baldwin** faces the vulnerable 4.62 xERA of Thornton. Both players are positioned to capitalize on their respective lineup spots, providing the stability needed to anchor our daily output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved selecting between **Andy Pages** (58.39) and the lower-projected **Heliot Ramos** (45.65). Despite the raw score difference, the volatility of the lineup order forced us to keep **Heliot Ramos** in the mix to preserve our depth, though his score remains marginal due to the difficulty of facing Miller. While **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung** remain sidelined on the IL, their absence continues to pinch our infield flexibility, making the contribution of **Nasim Nunez** (52.28) necessary despite a lower ceiling due to his bottom-of-the-order positioning. We are closely monitoring the weather and confirmed lineups for the late games, as any shift in the wind could significantly impact the power potential of **Kyle Tucker** (64.08) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.03) against their respective left-handed matchups. Given the scarcity of stolen bases, we are prioritizing **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** (61.47) to lead our offensive aggression, even with **Jackson Merrill** facing a tougher matchup against May.",
